# yard.epic: the flow of rig yard's epics (yardr rig flow yard --type epic
# yard.epic). An epic waits in open while its children are open (each child
# blocks it); once the last closes, yard-integrators rebases its branch onto
# main and gates it, Codex reviews the whole diff, and the epic lands on main
# either through a pull request (approved -> in-pr -> land, with YARDR_PR)
# or locally, where the refinery fast-forwards main and advances it straight
# to merged (the bare edge, which no outcome offers). See
# docs/pipeline.md#epics.
backlog -> open
open -> review on done | open on failed | backlog
review -> approved on done | open on changes | decide on question
approved -> in-pr on done | open on failed | merge on conflict | merged
in-pr -> land on done | open on changes | decide on question
land -> merged on done | open on failed
merge -> review on done | open on rework | decide on question
decide -> open | backlog
merged terminal
